## Fix 4 — OS-Level Screen Unlock (FR-01)

**Problem:** No actual Windows lock screen unlock.

#### [MODIFY] [command_executor.py](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/executor/command_executor.py)
- Add `_unlock_screen()`: use `ctypes.windll.user32.LockWorkStation` in reverse: send Ctrl+Alt+Del simulation via `pywinauto` or check screen state
- Add `_lock_screen()`: `ctypes.windll.user32.LockWorkStation()`
- Register `LOCK_SCREEN` and `UNLOCK_SCREEN` intents

#### [MODIFY] [command_parser.py](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/interpreter/command_parser.py)
- Parse: `"lock the screen"`, `"lock system"` → `LOCK_SCREEN`
- Parse: `"unlock system"`, `"unlock the screen"` → `UNLOCK_SCREEN` (requires Prime or passphrase)

