## Fix 5 — Voice Speaker Verification (FR-02, FR-03)

**Problem:** VoiceListener transcribes but doesn't verify who is speaking.

#### [NEW] [voice_profile_manager.py](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/security/voice_profile_manager.py)
- Use `resemblyzer` library (`pip install resemblyzer`)
- `enroll(audio_samples)` — save speaker embedding to `data/voice_profile.npy`
- [verify(audio_data)](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/security/passphrase_manager.py#22-29) → `bool` — compare new recording against stored embedding using cosine similarity (threshold: 0.75)

#### [MODIFY] [voice_listener.py](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/input/voice_listener.py)
- After STT, if `voice_profile` exists: run speaker verify before passing to callback
- If verification fails: speak "Voice not recognized" and drop command

#### [MODIFY] [orchestrator.py](file:///c:/Users/nithi/Desktop/MAX/max/max_core/core/orchestrator.py)
- Add `ENROLL_VOICE` intent (`"enroll my voice"`, `"train voice"`) to trigger enrollment flow
- After enrollment success, persist profile via `VoiceProfileManager`

